WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.210
- In fact when he does those
things, people freak out.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.390
Kids make fun of you, you're
an immigrant, you're poor.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:06.377
Winning's easy.

00:00:06.377 --> 00:00:08.427
Then I said, "Oh, make a profit
and all these other things."

00:00:08.427 --> 00:00:09.278
And he said, "No."

00:00:09.278 --> 00:00:11.416
My dad works in a factor sweeping floors,

00:00:11.416 --> 00:00:12.819
and my mom's a receptionist.

00:00:12.819 --> 00:00:16.481
People over-complicate
business and success.

00:00:16.481 --> 00:00:17.906
I always say to people, "I'm not

00:00:17.906 --> 00:00:19.782
"in business for emotional gratification."

00:00:19.782 --> 00:00:21.632
If you dropped me in
the middle of a jungle,

00:00:21.632 --> 00:00:22.966
I'll figure out a way to survive.

00:00:22.966 --> 00:00:24.400
And I say forget the lot of money part.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.701
Why were we put on this earth?

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:29.542
- He's a Croatian-born,
Canadian businessman,

00:00:29.542 --> 00:00:32.941
author, investor, and TV personality.

00:00:32.941 --> 00:00:34.269
Herjavec Group is one of Canada's

00:00:34.269 --> 00:00:36.519
fastest growing technology companies.

00:00:36.519 --> 00:00:39.963
He has an estimated net
worth of $200 million.

00:00:39.963 --> 00:00:41.326
He's Robert Herjavec and here are

00:00:41.326 --> 00:00:43.826
his top ten rules for success.

00:00:46.721 --> 00:00:49.035
- You have to be passionate about

00:00:49.035 --> 00:00:52.109
one thing, be great at one thing.

00:00:52.109 --> 00:00:56.276
The world will reward your
knowledge of a very narrow field.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.485
So the analogy I always use is, you know,

00:01:00.485 --> 00:01:02.893
Tom Brady, I love NFL football, Tom Brady

00:01:02.893 --> 00:01:06.122
gets paid $25 million a
year to throw the ball.

00:01:06.122 --> 00:01:09.859
He doesn't get paid to block,
he doesn't get paid to tackle.

00:01:09.859 --> 00:01:13.066
In fact, when he does those
things, people freak out.

00:01:13.066 --> 00:01:14.149
Be Tom Brady.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:16.307
- [Interviewer] Be good at...

00:01:16.307 --> 00:01:17.793
- Be good at one thing.
- One thing, that one thing.

00:01:17.793 --> 00:01:19.611
And then be great at that one thing.

00:01:19.611 --> 00:01:22.574
Be world class at one thing.

00:01:22.574 --> 00:01:24.760
Forget your weaknesses,
because somebody is

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.811
going to eat your lunch at
the stuff you're not good at.

00:01:27.811 --> 00:01:29.054
I'm a pretty happy guy
- Yeah.

00:01:29.054 --> 00:01:31.319
You know, I think that's
one of the keys to success.

00:01:31.319 --> 00:01:34.563
I read in an article that the
difference between successful

00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:37.083
people and people that struggle,

00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:39.783
are successful people exude joy.

00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:41.248
Jeff, if you're not a happy guy,

00:01:41.248 --> 00:01:42.081
and other people don't want to

00:01:42.081 --> 00:01:42.944
hang out with you,
- Right.

00:01:42.944 --> 00:01:43.785
Why would they hang out

00:01:43.785 --> 00:01:44.618
with you?
- Right.

00:01:44.618 --> 00:01:45.903
If you're miserable, and nobody wants

00:01:45.903 --> 00:01:49.023
to spend time with you, how are
you ever going to get ahead?

00:01:49.023 --> 00:01:50.223
- [Jeff] Yeah it's...
- Why complain?

00:01:50.223 --> 00:01:52.080
I remember when we were really young,

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.893
this lesson was taught to me by my dad,

00:01:53.893 --> 00:01:55.666
and I kind of had a
miserable day at school

00:01:55.666 --> 00:01:56.807
'cuz ya know, the kids make fun of you,

00:01:56.807 --> 00:01:58.433
you're an immigrant, you're poor,

00:01:58.433 --> 00:02:00.380
and I came home and I was
feeling sorry for myself,

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.166
and my dad came home, it's going to sound

00:02:02.166 --> 00:02:06.157
so melodramatic, he walked a
couple miles to the factory,

00:02:06.157 --> 00:02:07.748
he was a blue-collar guy and I came home,

00:02:07.748 --> 00:02:10.708
and he just stood there and I
was complaining about my day.

00:02:10.708 --> 00:02:11.898
- [Jeff] Where were you living?

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:15.480
- Oh, we were living in
like a, oh, this stage

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.605
would be three times the
size, in a little apartment.

00:02:17.605 --> 00:02:20.049
- [Jeff] Oh there's a, oh my gosh.

00:02:20.049 --> 00:02:22.932
- Oh it wasn't pleasant,
and my dad was just

00:02:22.932 --> 00:02:24.422
standing there and I was
complaining and feeling sorry

00:02:24.422 --> 00:02:27.973
for myself and my dad
looks at me and says,

00:02:27.973 --> 00:02:30.838
"Never complain, you
should always be happy

00:02:30.838 --> 00:02:32.489
"with the opportunities given you."

00:02:32.489 --> 00:02:34.225
And that was it, and so you...

00:02:34.225 --> 00:02:36.686
(audience applause)

00:02:36.686 --> 00:02:38.706
You feel that big.

00:02:38.706 --> 00:02:41.891
You know, every time
you lose at something,

00:02:41.891 --> 00:02:44.101
you're one step closing
to winning the next time.

00:02:44.101 --> 00:02:45.682
The difference between successful people

00:02:45.682 --> 00:02:47.255
and not successful people,
- Okay.

00:02:47.255 --> 00:02:48.647
let's call it that way,
- Sure.

00:02:48.647 --> 00:02:51.276
are people give up, people
wake up every morning,

00:02:51.276 --> 00:02:53.058
they have doubt, they have fear,

00:02:53.058 --> 00:02:56.214
they lose in a Ferrari race,
or they lose in a race,

00:02:56.214 --> 00:02:58.240
and then they just give up.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.045
But the hardest thing in
life to learn, is to lose.

00:03:01.045 --> 00:03:03.554
Winning's easy, you win, you're happy,

00:03:03.554 --> 00:03:05.504
you get a high five,
your friends are happy.

00:03:05.504 --> 00:03:07.500
It's your ability to take a loss,

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.287
get up the next day, dust
yourself off, and keep going.

00:03:10.287 --> 00:03:13.104
I have lost at everything
you can imagine, seriously.

00:03:13.104 --> 00:03:16.104
I have been beat up and put down and

00:03:17.728 --> 00:03:20.988
everything that can go
wrong, has gone wrong for me.

00:03:20.988 --> 00:03:22.558
But I just kept going.

00:03:22.558 --> 00:03:24.068
I used to work for Warren Avis,

00:03:24.068 --> 00:03:25.338
the guy who started Avis Rent a Car,

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.269
and he said to me one day, "Robert,

00:03:27.269 --> 00:03:28.438
"what's the purpose of business?"

00:03:28.438 --> 00:03:30.539
And I said, "Oh, make a profit,
and all these other things."

00:03:30.539 --> 00:03:32.866
And he said, "No, the purpose of business

00:03:32.866 --> 00:03:35.317
"is to create a customer because

00:03:35.317 --> 00:03:37.430
"everything else takes care of itself."

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:40.765
It you can create customers,
and create value for them,

00:03:40.765 --> 00:03:42.537
because the answer to
that question is different

00:03:42.537 --> 00:03:45.016
for every single customer, then

00:03:45.016 --> 00:03:46.605
you're going to have a great business.

00:03:46.605 --> 00:03:48.159
You know what's funny,
when I was growing up,

00:03:48.159 --> 00:03:49.818
everybody said that to me, "It's not what

00:03:49.818 --> 00:03:51.199
"you know, it's who you know."

00:03:51.199 --> 00:03:52.348
- [Jeff] Is that true?

00:03:52.348 --> 00:03:54.711
- Well, so there I am, I'm 18 years old,

00:03:54.711 --> 00:03:56.994
my dad works in a factory sweepin' floors,

00:03:56.994 --> 00:03:59.645
and my mom's a receptionist,
so if the key to success

00:03:59.645 --> 00:04:03.536
in life is who you know, I'm in trouble.

00:04:03.536 --> 00:04:04.656
(audience laughs)

00:04:04.656 --> 00:04:07.302
So I said to myself,
"I don't believe that.

00:04:07.302 --> 00:04:09.651
"I believe I got to go
out and become the guy

00:04:09.651 --> 00:04:11.350
"that others want to get to know."

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.405
(audience applause)

00:04:12.405 --> 00:04:13.943
- It's all about what you make of it.

00:04:13.943 --> 00:04:15.625
- And you listened to what you call

00:04:15.625 --> 00:04:19.868
your spidey senses or your
spider senses, your intuition.

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:21.801
- [Robert] All the time.
- Have you always?

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:25.356
- Always, always, I learned
that from my parents

00:04:25.356 --> 00:04:27.391
because I don't have a fancy education.

00:04:27.391 --> 00:04:29.722
We didn't have fancy advisors.

00:04:29.722 --> 00:04:32.826
The most successful
person I knew growing up

00:04:32.826 --> 00:04:35.377
was my dad's boss, and
that was only because

00:04:35.377 --> 00:04:39.124
he had more seniority in
the union than my dad.

00:04:39.124 --> 00:04:41.953
So you've got to learn
to listen to yourself.

00:04:41.953 --> 00:04:46.112
People over-complicate
business and success.

00:04:46.112 --> 00:04:47.928
People are watching right now and saying,

00:04:47.928 --> 00:04:49.546
"Oh I can't do what he does 'cuz

00:04:49.546 --> 00:04:50.970
"I don't know how to run a business."

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.887
Everybody has the ability, you

00:04:52.887 --> 00:04:55.387
just got to listen to yourself.

00:04:56.999 --> 00:04:58.644
- That's hard to do.
- Very hard.

00:04:58.644 --> 00:05:01.632
Because you get the message,
and it's unemotional,

00:05:01.632 --> 00:05:05.363
and you think, I know you
have to listen to your senses.

00:05:05.363 --> 00:05:08.270
When you're on an elevator,
a big hefty guy gets on,

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:11.985
as a female, get off, right, no matter

00:05:11.985 --> 00:05:15.641
if you're intuition is right,
just get off the elevator.

00:05:15.641 --> 00:05:19.808
- It's fear, I think most
people are blinded by fear.

00:05:21.509 --> 00:05:25.033
And to be successful at
anything, you've got to be able

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:27.474
to control that and work
your way through it.

00:05:27.474 --> 00:05:29.223
I always say to people,
"I'm not in business for

00:05:29.223 --> 00:05:33.097
"emotional gratification, I'm
in business to make money and

00:05:33.097 --> 00:05:35.445
"build a great company and
all these other things."

00:05:35.445 --> 00:05:37.734
So you got to leave your
emotion out of it, because

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:42.666
when you're angry, or you hate,
you make stupid decisions.

00:05:42.666 --> 00:05:44.423
But that doesn't mean you have to become

00:05:44.423 --> 00:05:47.361
a jerk, or mean about
it, I mean, nobody likes

00:05:47.361 --> 00:05:50.192
to do business with
somebody who isn't nice.

00:05:50.192 --> 00:05:52.349
- You draw on other people's experiences

00:05:52.349 --> 00:05:54.598
that don't seem to relate to your life.

00:05:54.598 --> 00:05:56.788
Georges St-Pierre, MMA fighter,

00:05:56.788 --> 00:05:59.132
what does a businessman learn from a guy

00:05:59.132 --> 00:06:01.757
who punches people for a living?

00:06:01.757 --> 00:06:03.901
- Well, we were just talking
about that outside and,

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:06.653
you know, the difference
between the UFC fighter and the

00:06:06.653 --> 00:06:10.326
rest of us, is no one hits
us in the face every morning.

00:06:10.326 --> 00:06:13.312
So that really brings things into focus.

00:06:13.312 --> 00:06:16.812
What I learned out of him is
it's all about being efficient.

00:06:16.812 --> 00:06:18.973
It's not the strong, it's not the big,

00:06:18.973 --> 00:06:20.427
it's not the rich, it's not the poor

00:06:20.427 --> 00:06:23.325
that'll inherit the Earth,
it'll be the efficient.

00:06:23.325 --> 00:06:25.311
You don't see too many
dinosaurs walking around anymore

00:06:25.311 --> 00:06:26.943
and they were really big animals.

00:06:26.943 --> 00:06:29.714
- So okay, great, so not being a dinosaur

00:06:29.714 --> 00:06:31.627
is an important lesson,
so how do you keep...

00:06:31.627 --> 00:06:34.889
- Adaptability, adaptability,
so I've never been

00:06:34.889 --> 00:06:36.952
the smartest guy in the room, but I feel

00:06:36.952 --> 00:06:38.859
pretty confident if you
dropped me in the middle

00:06:38.859 --> 00:06:41.078
of a jungle, I'll figure
out a way to survive.

00:06:41.078 --> 00:06:44.156
It's your ability to survive
in any situation that

00:06:44.156 --> 00:06:47.475
separates the people that do
well from those that don't.

00:06:47.475 --> 00:06:51.392
I think you've got to
find what makes you tick.

00:06:54.289 --> 00:06:57.093
And I think greatness comes from when you

00:06:57.093 --> 00:06:59.760
marry your passion with your job

00:07:01.385 --> 00:07:02.850
'cuz I don't really think I have a job,

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:05.583
I just, I love what I do, and
I always say that to kids.

00:07:05.583 --> 00:07:08.203
I talk to a lot of kids who
are university, and say,

00:07:08.203 --> 00:07:09.674
"How do I make a lot of money?"

00:07:09.674 --> 00:07:11.281
And I say, "Forget the lot of money part.

00:07:11.281 --> 00:07:13.575
"Find something you're
going to be great at,

00:07:13.575 --> 00:07:15.124
"and let the money follow you."

00:07:15.124 --> 00:07:18.371
- So what is it about people
who find their passion,

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:20.255
who work hard, and never make a dime?

00:07:20.255 --> 00:07:23.755
Well they make a few dimes but not enough?

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:25.532
They never get there.

00:07:25.532 --> 00:07:26.822
- So, you know, Fanny, it's interesting

00:07:26.822 --> 00:07:30.082
'cuz we have this
conversation all the time.

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:33.278
I live in a very affluent
area and I have these

00:07:33.278 --> 00:07:36.243
quarterly dinners, or I
used to, with my neighbors,

00:07:36.243 --> 00:07:38.725
so at one point I had 20 guys,

00:07:38.725 --> 00:07:40.353
they were all worth hundreds
of millions of dollars,

00:07:40.353 --> 00:07:42.410
and we asked that same question.

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:45.472
Can you always be successful, even if

00:07:45.472 --> 00:07:47.622
you love what you do
and all the other stuff?

00:07:47.622 --> 00:07:50.184
And the reality is, as my dad said,

00:07:50.184 --> 00:07:54.125
if you work hard, you will
never be poor in life.

00:07:54.125 --> 00:07:57.820
But just because you work hard,
doesn't mean you'll be rich.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:08:00.312
Sometimes you need to get lucky,

00:08:00.312 --> 00:08:02.721
but the reality is, that
the harder you work,

00:08:02.721 --> 00:08:04.596
it's true, the luckier you get.

00:08:04.596 --> 00:08:07.889
'Cuz people always think
there's a finality to success.

00:08:07.889 --> 00:08:09.505
You know, people think about success

00:08:09.505 --> 00:08:11.102
in terms of the finish line.

00:08:11.102 --> 00:08:13.417
People always ask me why
are you so successful?

00:08:13.417 --> 00:08:16.620
And I always correct them and
I say, "I'm not successful."

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.478
You know, the minute you think you've

00:08:18.478 --> 00:08:20.611
made it, is the beginning of the end.

00:08:20.611 --> 00:08:24.470
So it's just about,
the overall message is,

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.085
you got to keep going, you
got to love what you do,

00:08:27.085 --> 00:08:28.346
and you got to keep going.

00:08:28.346 --> 00:08:30.785
- [Interviewer] Why?

00:08:30.785 --> 00:08:32.434
- 'Cuz what's the alternative?

00:08:32.434 --> 00:08:33.553
What's the alternative?

00:08:33.553 --> 00:08:36.074
Why were we put on this earth?

00:08:36.074 --> 00:08:40.241
Were we put on this earth to
be miserable and to complain

00:08:41.744 --> 00:08:45.038
and to look at life as victims?

00:08:45.038 --> 00:08:49.710
I am in control of everything
that happens to me.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:53.677
Everything, everything that
will happen in my life,

00:08:53.677 --> 00:08:55.792
I will be the master of.

00:08:55.792 --> 00:08:57.993
That doesn't mean my life
will always be happy.

00:08:57.993 --> 00:09:00.439
That doesn't mean my
life will always be good.

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:03.772
But I have the ultimate choice to choose

00:09:05.273 --> 00:09:07.942
how I will react to the
things that happen to me,

00:09:07.942 --> 00:09:10.050
and move forward from them.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:13.467
And I'm okay with not succeeding at them,

00:09:14.831 --> 00:09:18.998
because the journey on that
road is worth it for me.

00:09:20.321 --> 00:09:21.472
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:09:21.472 --> 00:09:25.000
I made this video because
Pov Neeri Roth asked me to.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.682
So if there's a famous entrepreneur that

00:09:26.682 --> 00:09:28.492
you want me to profile next, leave it

00:09:28.492 --> 00:09:30.997
in the comments below and
I'll see what I can do.

00:09:30.997 --> 00:09:32.576
I'd also love to know
which of Robert Herjavec's

00:09:32.576 --> 00:09:35.385
top ten rules meant the most to you.

00:09:35.385 --> 00:09:37.787
Leave it in the comments and
I'll join the discussion.

00:09:37.787 --> 00:09:39.014
Thank you so much for watching.

00:09:39.014 --> 00:09:42.597
Continue to believe,
and I'll see you soon.

